WEBVTT

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:18.490
Karte 7 - Black and White

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.600
<i>Men... Do!</i>
(Note: Men = head strike
Do = torso strike)

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:40.840
All right, forearm blow!
Match over!

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:47.180
Ah, Yasuhiko.
You want to go next?

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.150
Yes, please.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:50.650
Nakamura! On the mat!

00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:51.660
Yes, sir!

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.390
One of this kendo team's
greatest former members...

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:56.760
has consented
to practice with us.

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:59.130
While enrolled here, he was...

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:00.360
the All-Japan champion
three years running!

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.640
Besides that, he graduated at the top
of his class in medical school!

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:08.330
He is now the chief of surgery
at Tozai University Hospital!

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:10.310
Mr. Yasuhiko Shirabyoshi!

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:19.180
What's wrong? Either you
make the first move or I will.

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:24.720
<i>Kote! Men! Men!</i>
(Note: Kote = forearm strike)

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:27.830
Thank you, sir!

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:29.430
Next!

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:30.960
If I may, sir!

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:33.460
<i>Men! Men! Men!</i>

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.740
We're home, Young Master.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:49.840
Hm? Oh.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:54.550
Welcome home, Young Master.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:57.890
Master Yasuhiko,
Miss Catherine is here.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.330
Mm. Okay.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:00.990
Sorry.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.430
For the wait, I mean.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:06.030
Don't worry. I came early.

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:10.360
Stopped by the university
gym again, huh?

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:14.240
Yeah. I get really wound up
after big operations.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.870
I can't sleep well
until I work up a good sweat.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:21.450
What's wrong? We've got the church
picked out for the ceremony.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:24.050
And the honeymoons
planned out perfectly.

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:26.920
Is there some other problem now?

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:31.480
Yasuhiko, I love you
with all my heart.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:34.090
And I love you, Catherine.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:36.500
But I'd like to put off our wedding
for one year...

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:39.190
No, for six months.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:44.970
But our plans...
What about all our plans...?

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:50.340
I'm sorry. I know how much
you hate to change any plan.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:53.310
But I've decided this
after a lot of thought!

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:57.380
I also resigned
from the dispensary today.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.880
I don't believe this...
You're just leaving?

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.860
I won't be near you
at work anymore!

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:08.090
Yasuhiko, listen to me!

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:11.790
You just said you love me,
and now you...!

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:14.260
Yasuhiko, hear me out!

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.260
Please, listen...

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:21.140
You've heard about the civil war
in Adentarl, right?

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:24.440
One group of people
is trying to seize power,

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.310
and innocent bystanders
have had their homes burned...

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.080
and have been injured
and killed in the process.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:36.220
Masses of sick and starving people
have gathered at the border.

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:40.490
What does that have to do
with our wedding?

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:45.360
When I became a doctor,
I also joined a volunteer group.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:49.170
You're not the
only member, right?

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:53.070
I've decided on my own.
It's now or never.

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:58.510
Because once I'm married
and carry your child,

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:02.380
I won't be able to rush off
on my own this easily anymore.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:08.460
Just six months. Will our love
fade in only six months?

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:10.780
No...

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:14.990
All right, now give me a kiss
and say, "see you later."

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:17.960
And as you miss me,
you can become...

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.260
a genius surgeon
with the highest ideals.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.740
See you later.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:27.940
You're finally feeling better.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.250
<i>To my darling</i>
<i>Yasuhiko Shirabyoshi,</i>

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:46.650
<i>It's been two weeks</i>
<i>since I arrived in Adentarl.</i>

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:51.230
<i>Conditions in the refugee camp</i>
<i>are worse than you can imagine.</i>

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:56.570
<i>Over 20 thousand people are crammed</i>
<i>into an area of only seven hectares.</i>

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:59.940
<i>Besides the treatment</i>
o<i>f the sick and wounded,</i>

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:02.310
<i>there's a shortage of food</i>
<i>and drinking water.</i>

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.640
<i>Each day we struggle</i>
<i>to replenish them.</i>

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.950
<i>Until help comes from the UN</i>
<i>and the Red Cross,</i>

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:10.780
<i>we all must work desperately.</i>

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:15.280
<i>By the way, we ran into</i>
<i>a mysterious person today...</i>

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:16.950
<i>out in the middle</i>
o<i>f the desert.</i>

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:25.400
<i>He was wearing a black coat</i>
<i>in the midday desert heat,</i>

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:27.260
<i>and his face</i>
<i>had a surgical scar.</i>

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:31.810
<i>He was also</i>
<i>carrying a medical bag.</i>

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:35.230
What's wrong?

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:39.910
As you can see, my engine
overheated and died on me.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.280
Where are you headed?

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:45.050
The refugee camp on the border.

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:49.810
Oh, then hop in.
We're on our way back there.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:51.380
I appreciate it.

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:53.150
Hold it!

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:58.960
Who are you?
What do you want at the camp?

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:02.930
What's in the bag?

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:04.700
Maybe it's a bomb!

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:08.670
Terrorists have threatened
to kill the refugees!

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:11.470
You think <i>I'm</i> a terrorist?

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:16.670
Oh, well...
Better find another taxi.

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:21.010
Wait! You want
to walk to the camp?

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:23.290
It's ten kilometers away!

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:30.050
<i>It was only later</i>
<i>that I learned who he was.</i>

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:32.260
<i>I'll get to that</i>
<i>in my next letter.</i>

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:36.200
Clinical Chart 7
White Justice

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:28.510
Even if you get caught up...

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:33.750
in the chaotic rhythms
of the city,

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:42.760
as long as you have
dreams you can't abandon,

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:50.710
it can't be all a loss.

00:07:53.950 --> 00:08:03.220
Even in a crowd,
you always keep to yourself.

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:08.660
She's gone to city lights.

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:13.160
It's because you don't understand
that you pretend to be so withdrawn.

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:15.940
She has gone to city lights.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:19.570
Even if you forsake the light,

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:23.870
you'll still be close.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:44.800
What's wrong, Catherine?

00:08:45.070 --> 00:08:46.690
<i>Ten kilometers</i>
<i>through the desert...</i>

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:51.240
<i>He didn't reach our camp</i>
<i>till late at night.</i>

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.540
Stop! Wait!

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:56.940
Don't take another step!

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:00.250
You're standing in a mine field!

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.610
Step back slowly
and follow your footprints!

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:16.860
Have the soup, too.
You need to warm up.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:20.600
It can drop below freezing
in the desert at night.

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:23.860
I appreciate it.

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:29.940
Walking here through the desert...
You must be crazy!

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:36.650
I went right out after you in
the truck, but I couldn't find you.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:37.710
Sorry about that.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:40.950
Are you all volunteers?

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:41.550
Yes.

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:44.450
I believe there's a girl
named Karen in this camp.

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:48.290
She's five years old
and is with her mother.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.890
If you know her, please tell me.

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:51.160
Karen?

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:54.790
Karen Aramis.
Her mother's name is Saranda.

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:56.300
Hang on a sec.

00:09:57.610 --> 00:10:00.070
There's another registry book.
Check that one, too!

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:00.730
Okay.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:04.410
Karen has
a hereditary heart condition...

00:10:04.550 --> 00:10:06.410
Tetralogy of Fallot.

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:07.910
She needs treatment.

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:10.580
You're a doctor?

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:16.260
By any chance... are you...?

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:24.430
Doctor, I'm begging you.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:27.590
You'll get
your million dollars.

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:31.600
Cash or transfer,
however you want it.

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:35.800
It's a hereditary heart disease
called Tetralogy of Fallot.

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:40.510
Swelling of the right ventricle,
which dislocates the aorta.

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:42.570
My granddaughter has it.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:45.250
She's like
a little angel to me.

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:48.220
I hear it's
very hard to treat.

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:51.950
All the other doctors
told me it's impossible.

00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:54.830
So, Doctor,
I'm begging you for help.

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:58.130
Hey, you bums!

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:00.790
Come on and beg the Doc with me!

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:02.590
Right, Boss!

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:09.370
We're beggin you!

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:14.910
I'm actually
from the Republic of Adentarl.

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:18.910
My daughter and granddaughter
live in the capital, Dentarl City.

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:26.790
<i>Attention. The shuttle bus</i>
<i>to Dentarl City will depart at...</i>

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:45.400
<i>Attention, all foreigners.</i>

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:47.140
<i>As of 1 1:00 today,</i>

00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:50.910
<i>Adentarl International Airport</i>
<i>is under military control.</i>

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:54.850
<i>All foreign entry visas</i>
<i>are now cancelled.</i>

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:59.120
<i>Foreigners must submit</i>
<i>to military authority.</i>

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:06.960
<i>My darling Yasuhiko, that doctor</i>
<i>escaped the military's hands...</i>

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:10.900
<i>and set off to Dentarl City</i>
<i>to meet his patient.</i>

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:17.740
<i>But the city was already</i>
<i>ravaged by the battle,</i>

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:20.440
<i>and its inhabitants had fled.</i>

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:24.540
<i>The patient he had to meet</i>
<i>and her family had disappeared.</i>

00:12:27.460 --> 00:12:30.690
<i>For the next two months,</i>
<i>he wandered Adentarl...</i>

00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:32.750
<i>amidst the civil war.</i>

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:37.160
<i>A scrap of information finally</i>
<i>led him to this refugee camp.</i>

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:41.530
<i>I'm so moved.</i>

00:12:42.270 --> 00:12:44.330
<i>I've never heard</i>
o<i>f a doctor...</i>

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:48.270
<i>so committed to a patient</i>
<i>as this one.</i>

00:12:53.110 --> 00:12:55.410
<i>These are the latest images</i>
<i>from the Republic of Adentarl.</i>

00:12:56.620 --> 00:12:58.350
<i>The civil war is still raging.</i>

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:02.080
<i>Refugee camps on the border</i>
<i>of neighboring Balique...</i>

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:03.560
<i>are nearly bursting.</i>

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:07.550
<i>And people fleeing the fighting</i>
<i>continue to gather there.</i>

00:13:08.230 --> 00:13:11.200
<i>A UN vote authorizing aid</i>
<i>is desperately needed.</i>

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:22.880
I don't believe it.

00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:27.310
He disappears for two months
without even giving me a phone call.

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:31.340
He might have gotten
in a bad accident.

00:13:31.390 --> 00:13:34.910
Or he's gotten really sick
and can't move.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:38.690
Or maybe he's cheating on me
with another woman!

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:41.850
Doctor!
What's happened to you?

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:43.650
Call me already!

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:45.660
Gimme a phone call!

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:47.530
One stupid phone call!

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:52.530
Coming! Coming!
Coming! Coming!

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:56.470
Doctor, where have you been?
I've been so lonely!

00:13:57.180 --> 00:14:00.310
Um, this is Mr. Patterson
in New York.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:03.950
You haven't heard
from the Doctor, have you?

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:07.110
Oh, great! Look, Mr. Patterson,
or Betterson, or whatever!

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:09.180
<i>I'm</i> the one who wants
the Doctor to call!

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:11.890
I see. You've heard nothing.

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:13.550
Sorry to bother you.

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:17.530
Boss! Cheer up!

00:14:17.570 --> 00:14:19.030
You're gonna
make yourself sick!

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:20.160
Clam up!

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:21.830
Sorry, Boss...

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:30.040
Here! Over here!

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:34.670
You've confirmed it?
There's no mistake?

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:39.550
They weren't in the registry,
but I heard talk about them.

00:14:39.590 --> 00:14:42.450
A dying little girl
and her half-crazy mother.

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:46.320
That's it. Let's pray.

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:51.490
That a great flock of doves
will come here,

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:56.090
and they'll bear us up
higher than the church roof.

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:59.700
Before long,
we'll see a great oasis.

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:02.970
We'll all gather there,
at the water's edge.

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:06.880
And we'll be greeted kindly...

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:09.950
Let's go there now,
Karen.

00:15:16.590 --> 00:15:22.690
Let me die! Karen's dead!
My little Karen is dead!

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:32.300
Who did you say was dead?

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:36.540
Madam, Karen isn't dead yet.

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:41.670
Pulse 120. Blood pressure 70.

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:43.240
Shock score of level two.

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:48.150
The Tetralogy of Fallot has caused
an oxygen deprivation seizure.

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:51.320
I'd like to operate
immediately.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:53.990
Can you guarantee me
light and a place to work?

00:15:54.030 --> 00:15:55.220
Yes, Doctor!

00:15:58.070 --> 00:15:59.860
Please, use our tent!

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:02.760
We can also offer
a small stock of medical supplies.

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:05.200
I'll assist you.

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:07.500
You're a doctor?

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:08.810
Yes. I graduated from...

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:10.570
the State University of New York
medical school,

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:12.840
and have been working
in the primary...

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:14.680
surgical department of
Tozai University Hospital.

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:16.440
If you're a surgeon,
I'd be eager for your help.

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:18.680
My pleasure, Doctor!

00:16:23.990 --> 00:16:25.190
-Hemoclamp.
-Yes, Doctor.

00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:28.430
I'm going to separate the fifth
and sixth ribs on the left side.

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:29.390
Ready a spreader.

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:31.920
Yes, Doctor. Standing by.

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:38.160
Now to get rid of the stenosis
of the pulmonary artery...

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:40.440
and then isolate the damage
to the ventricular septum.

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:41.300
Yes, Doctor.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:43.840
Increase procainamide.

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:45.310
Procainamide level is okay.

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:48.640
Please increase
the IV drip rate.

00:16:48.680 --> 00:16:49.740
R- Right!

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:57.550
That's it, Karen!
Nice and strong!

00:16:57.590 --> 00:16:59.650
That's the way...
Hang in there...

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:02.130
Suction.

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:02.920
Yes, Doctor.

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:11.360
-We're here, Young Master.
-Okay.

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:14.600
Hello, Doctor.

00:17:14.640 --> 00:17:15.470
Hello.

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:18.970
Hi...
So, two operations today?

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:22.840
Yes, sir. Removal of
a subdural hematoma at 10 A.M.,

00:17:22.880 --> 00:17:25.010
and a pituitary adenoma
in the afternoon.

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:26.280
Hm. Okay.

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:30.820
Oh, and how's Mr. Nagai
in Ward Three progressing?

00:17:31.390 --> 00:17:32.450
Extremely well.

00:17:33.060 --> 00:17:35.460
Okay, then give him
4500 cc of Dextrin G...

00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:36.620
and 40 mg of Xanbon.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:37.930
Yes, Doctor. Understood.

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:41.570
<i>Dear Yasuhik</i>o,

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:44.630
<i>It was a fantastic operation.</i>

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:48.900
<i>The facilities were poor,</i>
<i>the operating table makeshift.</i>

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:52.380
<i>Our light came from bare bulbs</i>
<i>powered by a portable generator.</i>

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:55.910
<i>Our IV was first-aid</i>
<i>saline solution bags.</i>

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:59.850
<i>And outside, a sandstorm blew</i>
<i>at 20 meters per second.</i>

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:03.690
<i>To a beginner like me,</i>
<i>who was used to having...</i>

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:07.460
<i>computerized assistance</i>
<i>and the latest medical equipment,</i>

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:10.930
<i>his surgery was</i>
<i>one surprise after another.</i>

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:14.300
<i>His scalpel technique</i>
<i>was unsurpassed.</i>

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:19.300
<i>And how he approached it, with</i>
<i>thorough knowledge of anatomy...</i>

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:23.140
Doctor, should we
increase the Predonine a bit?

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:27.500
We can't. Too much Predonine will
cause post-operative complications.

00:18:28.820 --> 00:18:31.310
Remember, we're dealing
with a five-year-old girl here!

00:18:31.350 --> 00:18:32.750
Right. Excuse me.

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:35.380
Sometimes you need to know
when not to use medicines.

00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:35.960
Right.

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:41.190
It's all right.
This girl's a fighter.

00:18:43.660 --> 00:18:44.460
Hang in there!

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:47.600
Yes, Doctor...

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:51.130
<i>He was strong, gentle...</i>

00:18:51.170 --> 00:18:55.110
<i>As that five-year-old girl's</i>
<i>life drained away,</i>

00:18:55.140 --> 00:18:59.580
<i>no one could have loved it more</i>
o<i>r tried harder to return it.</i>

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:03.550
<i>Perhaps he was holding onto it</i>
<i>through the entire operation.</i>

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:12.990
As overly-romantic as ever,
Catherine.

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:24.370
Romance can't save
a person’s life, you fool!

00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:28.810
Dr. Shirabyoshi, you should
get down to the OR.

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:30.240
Right. Okay.

00:19:33.450 --> 00:19:34.850
Who's assisting me today?

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:38.010
Doctors Tanaka and Toyama, sir.

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:39.210
Right!

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:43.250
<i>I think you've heard of him,</i>
<i>Yasuhiko.</i>

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:47.850
<i>He's the famous Dr. Black Jack.</i>

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:12.320
Madam, the operations
over for now.

00:20:12.950 --> 00:20:17.820
She'll need to recuperate
in a properly equipped hospital.

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:43.380
Doctor! Dr. Black Jack!

00:20:43.420 --> 00:20:45.510
Please wake up!
A helicopter's here!

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:53.790
I contacted Dr. Stanfield.

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:57.420
Stanfield?

00:20:58.030 --> 00:21:00.130
One of my professors
back in school.

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:05.100
He said he's very interested in
Tetralogy of Fallot cases.

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:08.470
He arranged for
a helicopter from New York.

00:21:09.380 --> 00:21:12.830
<i>Stanfield... An authority</i>
o<i>n cardiac surgery.</i>

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:15.110
Doctor, hurry!

00:21:27.330 --> 00:21:30.730
Excuse me, Doctor.
Can you look at my boy?

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:34.330
My girl stepped on a mine.
Can we do anything?

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:37.900
His fever won't go down,
and he has dysentery, too!

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:48.910
Doctor, you're the only
real surgeon we have here.

00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:52.980
Hey, Catherine!
What's wrong? Hurry up!

00:21:56.290 --> 00:22:02.590
Doctor! Dr. Stanfield said he'd see
to Karen’s recovery, so please...!

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:06.430
I didn't come here
as a volunteer!

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:07.600
Doctor!

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:10.970
I will not treat them
without compensation!

00:22:11.840 --> 00:22:17.180
Please! It won't be long
till the UN aid vote passes!

00:22:22.350 --> 00:22:23.870
One dollar per person!

00:22:24.550 --> 00:22:26.180
No discounts given!

00:22:26.750 --> 00:22:30.520
However, if you don't have
the money, I'll accept an IOU!

00:22:30.560 --> 00:22:31.490
Interest free!

00:22:33.090 --> 00:22:34.080
Doctor...!

00:22:35.830 --> 00:22:37.760
Give my regards
to Dr. Stanfield.

00:22:39.470 --> 00:22:40.400
I will!

00:22:44.540 --> 00:22:49.340
Careful! Watch her condition!
That's a young girl you have there!

00:22:57.650 --> 00:22:59.550
Boss! Boss!

00:23:00.150 --> 00:23:03.020
S- Someone here to see you, sir!

00:23:03.060 --> 00:23:06.190
Who? A detective?
A lawyer? The DA?

00:23:06.590 --> 00:23:08.460
Or some casino cheat?

00:23:08.500 --> 00:23:10.430
Um, no. Actually...

00:23:14.740 --> 00:23:16.760
You Patterson?

00:23:18.110 --> 00:23:19.500
You're the girl from the phone!

00:23:19.540 --> 00:23:21.010
Bingo! Bingo!

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:24.440
I'm Pinoko,
private secretary and assistant...

00:23:24.480 --> 00:23:26.880
to the genius surgeon Black Jack.

00:23:26.910 --> 00:23:29.470
And I have come
here to New York!

00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:33.110
Um... Um... Hold on here.

00:23:33.150 --> 00:23:38.250
What if, by some chance,
the Doc calls home? What'll you do?

00:23:38.290 --> 00:23:40.280
You should be home,
waiting for that!

00:23:42.260 --> 00:23:44.960
Relax. No problem!

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:48.060
I've had all calls
forwarded to this phone!

00:23:48.270 --> 00:23:50.240
Ain't modern conveniences great?

00:23:50.540 --> 00:23:51.530
Oh, I see.

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.270
<i>And now this breaking news.</i>

00:23:57.610 --> 00:24:00.480
<i>UN forces have</i>
<i>now entered Adentarl.</i>

00:24:03.680 --> 00:24:05.050
<i>They are intervening</i>
<i>in the civil war.</i>

00:24:06.120 --> 00:24:09.280
<i>This should end</i>
<i>hostilities there shortly.</i>

00:24:09.820 --> 00:24:11.620
They did it! They did it!

00:24:12.430 --> 00:24:15.050
Please, Miss. Eat all you like.

00:24:15.730 --> 00:24:18.890
Once the war's over,
the Doc will come back.

00:24:18.930 --> 00:24:22.390
I asked him to operate on
my granddaughter in Adentarl.

00:24:22.440 --> 00:24:26.000
It's all my fault. I never thought
a civil war would break out!

00:24:26.040 --> 00:24:28.010
I'm really sorry about
putting him through that.

00:24:29.080 --> 00:24:33.540
I heard he even stayed behind
as a volunteer.

00:24:34.380 --> 00:24:35.580
Well, I sent him to
where the patient was.

00:24:35.620 --> 00:24:38.310
I never promised
it would be completely safe.

00:24:38.350 --> 00:24:40.050
I'm full!

00:24:43.090 --> 00:24:47.420
Please, Miss. You have
to meet my granddaughter Karen.

00:24:47.460 --> 00:24:49.900
She's hospitalized
here in New York.

00:24:49.930 --> 00:24:53.420
You and she would probably
get along great!

00:24:53.470 --> 00:24:54.990
Hm... How old is she?

00:24:55.040 --> 00:24:56.130
Five.

00:24:56.170 --> 00:24:59.660
Nah. I only get along
with people over 1 7.

00:24:59.710 --> 00:25:02.570
And then only if it's
a really cute guy.

00:25:05.110 --> 00:25:05.740
Oh, well.

00:25:08.550 --> 00:25:11.710
Good morning, Karen.
How are you feeling?

00:25:12.150 --> 00:25:14.780
Good morning, Dr. Catherine!

00:25:15.360 --> 00:25:17.020
And Dr. Stanfield.

00:25:17.860 --> 00:25:19.220
I feel great!

00:25:19.990 --> 00:25:23.450
She had no fever last night
and slept soundly.

00:25:26.300 --> 00:25:29.790
Hmm... Nice steady pulse.

00:25:30.040 --> 00:25:32.230
Okay, can you stick out
your tongue for me?

00:25:33.610 --> 00:25:35.540
My, what a long tongue you have!

00:25:36.440 --> 00:25:39.280
I can touch the tip
of my nose with it!

00:25:39.310 --> 00:25:40.680
My, that's amazing!

00:25:41.620 --> 00:25:44.580
Catherine, do you have the notes
from Dr. Black Jack's surgery?

00:25:44.620 --> 00:25:45.950
Yes. Right here, sir.

00:25:47.220 --> 00:25:49.090
All right then. Karen?

00:25:49.120 --> 00:25:51.720
May I see that lovely scar
on your chest?

00:25:52.060 --> 00:25:52.820
'Kay!

00:25:54.760 --> 00:25:56.230
Oh! Dr. Catherine!

00:25:58.100 --> 00:25:59.730
Phone call for you.

00:25:59.770 --> 00:26:01.600
I see...

00:26:01.640 --> 00:26:03.190
<i>When do you get off work?</i>

00:26:03.240 --> 00:26:03.760
Huh?

00:26:04.540 --> 00:26:06.870
<i>Shall we have</i>
<i>pasta for lunch or hot dogs?</i>

00:26:08.510 --> 00:26:09.440
Oh, my!

00:26:09.580 --> 00:26:13.210
Jeez, it's about time
you recognized my voice.

00:26:18.320 --> 00:26:20.310
I took a two-week leave.

00:26:20.350 --> 00:26:22.320
To see you, of course.

00:26:22.760 --> 00:26:24.880
Oh, that was a big sacrifice.

00:26:24.930 --> 00:26:27.220
A doctor can't spare two weeks.

00:26:27.260 --> 00:26:29.350
The surgical department
must be in chaos now.

00:26:29.400 --> 00:26:32.230
They all depend on you.

00:26:32.270 --> 00:26:36.700
If a patient dies while I'm away,
it'll be your fault.

00:26:36.740 --> 00:26:37.530
Don't say that!

00:26:39.210 --> 00:26:41.230
Oh, my goodness.
Now what'll I do?

00:26:41.280 --> 00:26:44.510
I'm kidding.
Dr. Stanfield called me out here.

00:26:44.540 --> 00:26:45.270
The Doctor did?

00:26:45.750 --> 00:26:47.980
Yeah. He's called
a special meeting of...

00:26:48.020 --> 00:26:50.070
the International
Medical Association.

00:26:50.950 --> 00:26:53.280
If you hadn't been here,
I would have...

00:26:53.320 --> 00:26:56.050
faxed over my apology
for not attending.

00:27:00.660 --> 00:27:01.560
Grandpa!

00:27:01.930 --> 00:27:03.020
Hi, Papa!

00:27:03.660 --> 00:27:06.530
Okay, Karen.
You're gonna have fun today!

00:27:07.230 --> 00:27:10.570
Let me present
my little friend, Miss Pinoko!

00:27:11.140 --> 00:27:14.570
Dum-da-dum! Ta-da-da-DAA!

00:27:14.610 --> 00:27:17.170
<i>Ta-da-da-DAA!</i>

00:27:17.210 --> 00:27:20.770
Out, you bums! Out!
Outta the hospital room!

00:27:23.380 --> 00:27:29.320
Once upon a time,
there was a boy and a girl.

00:27:29.360 --> 00:27:32.880
The boy had long hair
dyed brown and an earring.

00:27:32.930 --> 00:27:36.050
And the girl liked drugs
and was bulimic...

00:27:36.100 --> 00:27:39.090
so her autonomic nerves
got all out of whack!

00:27:40.530 --> 00:27:44.060
But they loved each other a lot,

00:27:44.100 --> 00:27:45.870
and thought they'd
want to stay together,

00:27:45.910 --> 00:27:49.070
even though their place
was really small.

00:27:50.310 --> 00:27:52.870
It's kind of a sad story,
ya know?

00:27:53.280 --> 00:27:56.440
The boy became
a street thug in the city,

00:27:56.480 --> 00:28:00.390
while the girl worked a register
in a little convenience store.

00:28:01.250 --> 00:28:05.120
My girlfriend works
a register in a little gas station!

00:28:05.160 --> 00:28:06.390
Who cares!

00:28:06.430 --> 00:28:08.990
Shut up
and listen to the story!

00:28:09.030 --> 00:28:13.160
One day, the boy
stopped calling the girl,

00:28:13.200 --> 00:28:15.330
and the girl just fell apart.

00:28:15.870 --> 00:28:20.030
"Oh, I miss him.
I miss him! I miss him!"

00:28:20.070 --> 00:28:21.900
DOCTOR, I MISS YOU!

00:28:21.940 --> 00:28:23.410
Which doctor?

00:28:42.430 --> 00:28:44.060
Dr. Black Jack?

00:28:45.900 --> 00:28:47.420
You're finally here.

00:28:47.970 --> 00:28:50.990
I've waited here every day
for two months for you to arrive.

00:28:51.340 --> 00:28:53.640
My boss wouldn't hear
any excuses about this.

00:29:00.110 --> 00:29:02.910
We've done it, Boss! He's here!

00:29:03.280 --> 00:29:07.620
Finally! You treat
that doctor well, ya hear me?

00:29:08.620 --> 00:29:10.560
He's here? The Doctor's here?

00:29:10.990 --> 00:29:13.390
Yes! I'm happy to say
he's arrived!

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:24.600
I'm sorry I haven't
kept in touch, Doctor.

00:29:25.370 --> 00:29:28.970
Dr. Shirabyoshi! You're right,
it has been too long!

00:29:29.010 --> 00:29:30.740
Dr. Stanfield!

00:29:30.780 --> 00:29:34.440
Dr. Robbins! Sorry to call you
out here from Sydney.

00:29:35.420 --> 00:29:37.280
All right, to the meeting hall!

00:29:37.850 --> 00:29:40.820
A light lunch has
been prepared for you.

00:29:48.960 --> 00:29:53.700
This is Dr. Catherine,
who will be assisting me today.

00:29:54.300 --> 00:29:56.000
A pleasure to meet you all.

00:30:02.340 --> 00:30:03.780
Dr. Black Jack!

00:30:05.450 --> 00:30:07.280
Dr. Black Jack?

00:30:07.450 --> 00:30:10.710
That's right, Karen.
This is Dr. Black Jack.

00:30:10.750 --> 00:30:12.780
The man who
saved your life.

00:30:13.520 --> 00:30:15.820
He really <i>is</i> like Lapandu!

00:30:16.160 --> 00:30:17.250
Lapandu?

00:30:17.290 --> 00:30:18.520
What's that?

00:30:19.930 --> 00:30:23.090
A legendary desert hero
in Adentarl.

00:30:24.660 --> 00:30:28.500
He wandered the desert
like the wind, riding a white horse.

00:30:28.540 --> 00:30:31.000
He saved many people
from troubles,

00:30:31.040 --> 00:30:33.510
and he's considered a desert god
who protects our land.

00:30:34.510 --> 00:30:37.270
Wow, that's so <i>cool!</i>

00:30:38.110 --> 00:30:40.580
Thank you, my Lapandu.

00:30:40.610 --> 00:30:42.640
My Lapandu!

00:30:43.980 --> 00:30:47.150
Karen, I'm not your Lapandu.

00:30:47.920 --> 00:30:50.480
That would be Mr. Patterson,
your grandfather.

00:30:52.460 --> 00:30:55.590
He paid a very large
medical fee to save you.

00:30:56.360 --> 00:31:01.390
And even now, he prays with all
his heart for you to get well.

00:31:05.540 --> 00:31:09.030
Now, would you remove
your gown? I have work to do.

00:31:11.780 --> 00:31:12.540
Boss!

00:31:12.580 --> 00:31:14.310
Boss, you okay?

00:31:14.450 --> 00:31:17.940
Turn up the heat!
You want me to catch a cold?

00:31:17.980 --> 00:31:20.150
Yes, sir! Right away! Sorry!

00:31:23.260 --> 00:31:25.250
Am I getting sick now?

00:31:27.090 --> 00:31:28.620
Now then, doctors.

00:31:29.360 --> 00:31:32.530
As head of the International
Medical Association,

00:31:32.570 --> 00:31:35.630
I've called
this emergency meeting.

00:31:35.670 --> 00:31:40.630
First, my apologies for
interrupting your busy schedules.

00:31:41.140 --> 00:31:43.700
Quite all right, Dr. Stanfield.

00:31:44.040 --> 00:31:48.070
Yes. If not for these,
we'd never get to see you.

00:31:48.980 --> 00:31:51.710
It's good to see you
looking well, Doctor!

00:31:51.750 --> 00:31:54.850
Oh, my. Thank you so much!
You flatter me, really.

00:31:55.620 --> 00:31:59.350
You said this concerns
international medical licensing?

00:31:59.760 --> 00:32:04.090
I believe you're all familiar with
a doctor by the name of Black Jack.

00:32:15.780 --> 00:32:20.910
There isn't anyone in the field
of medicine who hasn't heard of him.

00:32:20.950 --> 00:32:22.140
The unlicensed doctor.

00:32:23.080 --> 00:32:25.020
I have encountered him.

00:32:25.620 --> 00:32:27.810
Or, more precisely,

00:32:28.720 --> 00:32:31.950
I have observed his work.

00:32:31.990 --> 00:32:33.690
And I have been moved!

00:32:38.200 --> 00:32:40.330
First of all,
have a look at this.

00:32:42.440 --> 00:32:46.630
The subject is a 5-year-old girl
with Tetralogy of Fallot.

00:32:46.670 --> 00:32:49.070
Observe his brilliant
and radical cure!

00:33:02.020 --> 00:33:06.390
Doctor, what hospital
do you work at?

00:33:07.730 --> 00:33:10.720
Well, I don't work at
any particular hospital.

00:33:11.130 --> 00:33:14.160
Darn it. Next time
I get a cold, I want to go...

00:33:14.200 --> 00:33:17.140
to the hospital
where you work!

00:33:17.500 --> 00:33:18.270
Forgive me.

00:33:18.810 --> 00:33:21.800
I want to be
your girlfriend someday!

00:33:28.880 --> 00:33:30.680
Madam, I'll be back tomorrow.

00:33:31.180 --> 00:33:33.620
She's doing well,
but there's still some risk...

00:33:33.650 --> 00:33:35.480
of postoperative
venous blood clotting.

00:33:35.790 --> 00:33:37.620
Yes, Doctor. By all means.

00:33:39.360 --> 00:33:42.560
Getting a cold, Pinoko?
Maybe you need an injection.

00:33:44.460 --> 00:33:46.400
Or perhaps
you need an enema.

00:33:46.430 --> 00:33:49.600
No! No way!

00:33:57.210 --> 00:34:00.540
Black Jack.
Real name: Kuro Hazama.

00:34:00.850 --> 00:34:03.040
This is his brilliant work.

00:34:03.450 --> 00:34:07.550
Performed, I might add,
under harsh conditions...

00:34:07.590 --> 00:34:09.020
in a refugee camp!

00:34:09.660 --> 00:34:11.850
See how he dealt
with the pulmonary artery,

00:34:11.890 --> 00:34:14.420
the most difficult segment
in any cardiac surgery.

00:34:14.460 --> 00:34:17.590
See the precise incisions
and sutures, all done...

00:34:17.630 --> 00:34:19.360
without the benefit
of an electric scalpel.

00:34:20.930 --> 00:34:26.270
This surgery is more perfect
than any I have ever seen!

00:34:26.910 --> 00:34:30.100
To be honest,
as a doctor, I'm jealous.

00:34:30.340 --> 00:34:33.210
And, while this is just a rumor,

00:34:33.250 --> 00:34:37.440
some of you here have
commissioned Mr. Black Jack...

00:34:37.480 --> 00:34:39.040
for difficult operations.

00:34:39.090 --> 00:34:40.520
More than a few!

00:34:43.660 --> 00:34:45.990
Now, to our discussion.

00:34:47.160 --> 00:34:52.190
I would like to grant Mr. Black Jack
an international medical license.

00:34:58.100 --> 00:35:00.700
Medical treatment now
is very advanced,

00:35:00.740 --> 00:35:02.500
but growing more specialized.

00:35:02.880 --> 00:35:04.710
"Look at the organs,
not the person."

00:35:04.740 --> 00:35:08.040
"Research over treatment."
That's the current way of thinking.

00:35:09.050 --> 00:35:13.540
We stress experimental results at
the cellular and molecular level...

00:35:13.590 --> 00:35:14.610
over actual treatment.

00:35:15.560 --> 00:35:20.790
In evaluating and recognizing
Mr. Black Jack's work,

00:35:20.830 --> 00:35:24.630
the IMA will cast the first stone
at this terrible trend in medicine!

00:35:25.230 --> 00:35:29.100
Of course, this would bring
his ingenious medical techniques...

00:35:29.140 --> 00:35:30.330
to the world at large.

00:35:30.370 --> 00:35:33.170
Think of how they'd be
perfected by doctors...

00:35:33.210 --> 00:35:34.870
on the front lines of treatment!

00:35:34.910 --> 00:35:38.900
It is with that thought
that I take this first step!

00:35:39.350 --> 00:35:41.710
If our committee is unanimous,

00:35:41.750 --> 00:35:43.740
then this agenda
will be recognized!

00:35:44.280 --> 00:35:46.120
Ladies and gentlemen,
your opinions?

00:35:49.660 --> 00:35:55.060
True, by licensing him, we'd be able
to request his services openly.

00:35:55.630 --> 00:35:58.390
We wouldn't have to sneak him
into hospitals anymore.

00:35:59.200 --> 00:36:03.430
And he might have to charge
standard rates to examine people.

00:36:04.540 --> 00:36:07.470
My hospital could accept him
as chief of surgery!

00:36:10.010 --> 00:36:10.910
Madness...

00:36:13.750 --> 00:36:15.870
You've all gone mad.

00:36:18.020 --> 00:36:23.010
Before our association can
grant him a license,

00:36:23.060 --> 00:36:26.360
he must first clear himself
of wrongdoing!

00:36:27.090 --> 00:36:31.620
An unlicensed doctor is
an affront to the rules of society!

00:36:31.660 --> 00:36:34.530
And the huge sums he charges
are a blasphemy...

00:36:34.570 --> 00:36:36.800
against patients
and legitimate doctors like us!

00:36:37.600 --> 00:36:39.200
Medicine is justice!

00:36:39.610 --> 00:36:43.240
The white clothes we wear
symbolize its pure, white justice!

00:36:43.880 --> 00:36:46.000
In regards to countless
peoples' lives,

00:36:46.050 --> 00:36:49.670
medicine's guiding principle
is fairness and justice, is it not?

00:36:50.350 --> 00:36:51.820
Dr. Shirabyoshi...

00:36:52.750 --> 00:36:54.580
My condition is
that he submit himself...

00:36:54.620 --> 00:36:57.610
to judgment by the law
for his crimes!

00:37:07.970 --> 00:37:11.530
Your opinion is sound,
with no room for compromise.

00:37:12.510 --> 00:37:17.700
But... But can't we change
your mind, Dr. Shirabyoshi?

00:37:18.880 --> 00:37:23.680
There's no one short of God Himself
who could judge him!

00:37:24.150 --> 00:37:27.280
How shameless!
An unlicensed doctor...

00:37:27.320 --> 00:37:29.290
just expects us
to give him a license?

00:37:29.320 --> 00:37:33.380
No, Mr. Black Jack knows
nothing of this discussion.

00:37:35.800 --> 00:37:39.530
This is still a dream
I've selfishly sketched out...

00:37:39.570 --> 00:37:42.590
for an unlicensed genius
I barely know.

00:37:42.640 --> 00:37:46.500
A desire to do something
for the physicians yet to come!

00:37:48.440 --> 00:37:52.310
I will call a meeting in one month
for your decision.

00:37:52.350 --> 00:37:57.080
I hope to have Mr. Black Jack with me
when that happens.

00:37:58.850 --> 00:38:01.340
Thank you all for coming today.

00:38:03.260 --> 00:38:06.250
C'mon, Doc. Just say the word!

00:38:06.590 --> 00:38:09.150
After all, you saved
my little Karen!

00:38:09.700 --> 00:38:12.960
I'll take you out to any nightclub
or casino you want!

00:38:13.700 --> 00:38:17.190
How about we go to "Double O,"
that hot new shabu-shabu place?

00:38:18.370 --> 00:38:19.240
Ta-daa!

00:38:19.570 --> 00:38:21.540
All right, I got it!

00:38:22.280 --> 00:38:24.570
All set, Doc. C'mon, let's go.

00:38:24.610 --> 00:38:26.100
First stop, a karaoke pub!

00:38:26.150 --> 00:38:28.710
No way! Three more hands, first!

00:38:32.650 --> 00:38:34.050
Take a drink!

00:38:34.090 --> 00:38:36.060
Dreamin' of California!

00:38:36.090 --> 00:38:37.390
Sing a song!

00:38:37.420 --> 00:38:39.450
Very nice baby, yeah!

00:38:39.490 --> 00:38:40.390
Raise some hell!

00:38:41.090 --> 00:38:44.260
Okay, Doc. Your turn.
Pick your favorite!

00:38:44.300 --> 00:38:46.460
No way! I hate karaoke!

00:38:46.870 --> 00:38:50.320
I know your type. Once you
start singing, you won't stop!

00:38:50.900 --> 00:38:51.840
Yay!

00:38:51.870 --> 00:38:53.930
Sing and dance around!

00:38:53.970 --> 00:38:58.600
When you're sick, (Sing!)
When you're well... (Raise hell!)

00:38:59.010 --> 00:38:59.980
Willy's gang!

00:39:19.130 --> 00:39:20.330
Dr. Black Jack!

00:39:25.970 --> 00:39:28.460
Papa! Papa!

00:39:28.510 --> 00:39:30.370
Papa! Papa!

00:39:31.080 --> 00:39:32.870
About that matter
we discussed on the phone...

00:39:33.580 --> 00:39:38.350
Yes. Dr. Stanfield has approved
your use of an operating room here.

00:39:38.380 --> 00:39:40.910
Thank you. I know
it's a sudden request.

00:39:40.950 --> 00:39:42.440
No, it's nothing.

00:39:43.260 --> 00:39:46.590
The patient took two shots
to the head, four to the abdomen.

00:39:47.060 --> 00:39:49.550
I need immediate X-rays.
I want to find those bullets.

00:39:49.600 --> 00:39:50.790
Of course, Doctor.

00:39:50.830 --> 00:39:52.260
And, Dr. Catherine?

00:39:52.300 --> 00:39:53.090
Yes?

00:39:53.700 --> 00:39:56.970
I'd appreciate it
if you assisted me again.

00:39:57.440 --> 00:40:01.460
Of course! I was going
to ask you if I could!

00:40:04.010 --> 00:40:06.910
The OR's in Room One
of the special center.

00:40:12.950 --> 00:40:15.180
Doctor, please put on
this surgical gown.

00:40:15.990 --> 00:40:17.850
-Here's yours, Miss Pinoko.
-Okay!

00:40:18.360 --> 00:40:21.690
Forgive me, but this hospital
practically belongs to...

00:40:21.730 --> 00:40:23.630
Dr. Stanfield, one of the great
elders of the medical world.

00:40:24.260 --> 00:40:26.060
I can't allow
illegal activity here.

00:40:28.100 --> 00:40:29.130
Yasuhiko...

00:40:29.670 --> 00:40:33.440
Can you please show me
your license, Dr. Black Jack?

00:40:35.680 --> 00:40:37.800
The Doctor authorized this!

00:40:38.210 --> 00:40:42.200
Quiet! I'm talking
to this fraud!

00:40:45.820 --> 00:40:47.340
I have no license.

00:40:47.390 --> 00:40:51.550
Then I will operate
on Mr. Patterson instead.

00:40:51.590 --> 00:40:54.750
This may be
a very difficult surgery.

00:40:55.190 --> 00:40:57.490
Relax. <i>I'm</i> a doctor!

00:41:09.640 --> 00:41:13.170
<i>My God! A bullet's lodged between</i>
<i>his brainstem and his cerebellum!</i>

00:41:13.780 --> 00:41:18.220
<i>It's impossible! If I scar</i>
<i>the myelencephalon with my scalpel,</i>

00:41:18.250 --> 00:41:20.720
<i>I'll stop the patient's</i>
<i>autonomic functions!</i>

00:41:21.390 --> 00:41:23.290
<i>This operation's impossible!</i>

00:41:24.920 --> 00:41:26.950
Dr. Shirabyoshi! We're ready!

00:41:27.290 --> 00:41:29.060
Right. Okay...

00:41:40.310 --> 00:41:43.400
Dr. Black Jack. At last, we meet.

00:41:44.180 --> 00:41:45.410
-Hemoclamp!
-Yes, sir.

00:41:46.210 --> 00:41:47.040
Blood pressure?

00:41:47.080 --> 00:41:48.940
80 over 50, and falling.

00:41:49.350 --> 00:41:51.370
Add 8 mg of Noradrenaline
to the IV!

00:41:51.420 --> 00:41:53.210
Adding 8 mg
of Noradrenaline to IV.

00:41:54.620 --> 00:41:57.750
He's cutting into
the fourth ventricle horoid plexus?

00:41:57.790 --> 00:41:59.050
Yes.

00:41:59.090 --> 00:42:00.560
That's terribly risky.

00:42:01.090 --> 00:42:02.560
Prepare for microsurgery!

00:42:03.160 --> 00:42:04.530
Yes, Doctor. Ready.

00:42:05.000 --> 00:42:06.730
Sorry about this.

00:42:06.770 --> 00:42:10.170
Shirabyoshi's young
and extremely talented,

00:42:10.200 --> 00:42:11.570
but he's uncompromising, too.

00:42:25.690 --> 00:42:28.980
Grandpa...
Is my grandpa gonna die?

00:42:29.620 --> 00:42:31.450
It’ll be all right, Karen.

00:42:32.090 --> 00:42:35.460
An excellent young doctor
is helping him now.

00:42:36.800 --> 00:42:40.790
And another excellent doctor
is here watching over him.

00:42:43.340 --> 00:42:46.000
No other surgeon
would be here...

00:42:46.040 --> 00:42:49.410
after having his patient
stolen from him.

00:42:51.780 --> 00:42:52.870
<i>Damn it all...!</i>

00:42:54.510 --> 00:42:56.740
<i>I've got bleeding from</i>
<i>the posterior cerebral artery!</i>

00:42:57.850 --> 00:43:01.340
<i>Don't panic! We're almost</i>
<i>into the fourth ventricle.</i>

00:43:03.860 --> 00:43:07.520
<i>It'll be all right! I've never cut</i>
<i>into the fourth ventricle before,</i>

00:43:07.560 --> 00:43:10.290
<i>but I've studied it thoroughly!</i>
<i>I can do this!</i>

00:43:15.900 --> 00:43:16.660
Doctor?

00:43:18.170 --> 00:43:21.440
<i>Dammit! I'm going to cut</i>
<i>the myelencephalon!</i>

00:43:22.070 --> 00:43:24.300
<i>Calm down! You can do this!</i>

00:43:25.750 --> 00:43:26.470
Not bad.

00:43:27.950 --> 00:43:30.750
Not bad, but the heat
of an electric scalpel there...

00:43:30.780 --> 00:43:33.120
will damage
the myelencephalors structure.

00:43:36.090 --> 00:43:38.890
Skill is necessary,
but experience is more vital here.

00:43:41.230 --> 00:43:45.390
And the point of this is
to save the patient, is it not?

00:43:50.940 --> 00:43:52.030
Dr. Black Jack...

00:43:54.110 --> 00:43:55.000
Hemoclamp!

00:43:55.040 --> 00:43:55.940
Yes, Doctor!

00:43:59.550 --> 00:44:00.640
How're his vitals?

00:44:01.280 --> 00:44:02.340
Not good!

00:44:04.480 --> 00:44:06.680
Concentrate on maintaining
his general condition.

00:44:06.720 --> 00:44:07.650
Agreed!

00:44:20.200 --> 00:44:21.360
Now I see...

00:44:22.500 --> 00:44:24.630
Operations aren't
for the surgeons benefit.

00:44:25.640 --> 00:44:28.900
And a surgeons honor
or qualifications don't matter.

00:44:30.310 --> 00:44:32.610
It's all about
saving the patient's life.

00:44:33.410 --> 00:44:36.710
Maybe I lost sight of that...

00:44:37.850 --> 00:44:38.820
Yasuhiko...

00:44:40.250 --> 00:44:42.620
For whose sake
will our wedding be?

00:44:47.290 --> 00:44:49.730
For the both of us,
of course.

00:44:53.930 --> 00:44:56.800
Shall we do it
a little sooner than planned?

00:44:59.270 --> 00:45:01.760
<i>Thursday, one month later.</i>

00:45:02.810 --> 00:45:06.710
<i>The second special meeting</i>
o<i>f the IMA was held.</i>

00:45:07.580 --> 00:45:11.020
<i>The motion to grant Mr. Black Jack</i>
<i>a medical license...</i>

00:45:11.420 --> 00:45:13.320
<i>was passed unanimously.</i>

00:45:14.420 --> 00:45:19.080
<i>But the medical genius</i>
<i>who needed the license,</i>

00:45:19.130 --> 00:45:20.960
<i>despite having</i>
<i>been invited to attend,</i>

00:45:21.790 --> 00:45:23.590
<i>and despite the hopes</i>
o<i>f those gathered there,</i>

00:45:24.230 --> 00:45:28.260
<i>never appeared at the meeting.</i>

00:45:32.610 --> 00:45:35.200
Doctor! Doctor!

00:45:35.880 --> 00:45:38.000
What's in this thing?

00:45:41.680 --> 00:45:44.910
Look at all these
IOUs for one dollar!

00:45:45.650 --> 00:45:47.020
Hm? Oh...

00:45:47.890 --> 00:45:51.690
I'll put these out
with the other burnable trash!

00:45:53.030 --> 00:45:53.680
Wha... Hey!

00:45:54.490 --> 00:45:56.620
Sorry. These are important.

00:45:57.460 --> 00:45:58.430
Huh?

00:46:05.070 --> 00:46:06.000
Good night.

00:46:47.110 --> 00:46:54.990
Can we go on with my heart
rusted over like this?

00:46:55.620 --> 00:46:58.020
Hey, baby...

00:46:58.060 --> 00:47:03.520
I envy
your light-hearted love.

00:47:06.070 --> 00:47:12.440
This cold city...
(Hey, baby.)

00:47:14.640 --> 00:47:19.580
Fades away
at the touch of moonlight.

00:47:21.050 --> 00:47:24.740
It's no good being alone.

00:47:25.890 --> 00:47:29.840
If you look,

00:47:30.120 --> 00:47:33.020
there's power to be found
in a gamble.

00:47:34.330 --> 00:47:38.130
It seems all over.

00:47:38.530 --> 00:47:41.830
Just like blackjack--
game over.

00:47:42.800 --> 00:47:46.360
Once you place your bet,
it's game over.

00:47:47.210 --> 00:47:50.000
I'd rather forget...

00:47:51.310 --> 00:47:54.140
my hopeful heart...

00:47:54.180 --> 00:47:56.810
in the midnight hours.

00:47:59.520 --> 00:48:01.490
Midnight hours.
